        "math_academy_id": "q-94149",
        "problem": "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}+38{x}_{2}^{2}+16{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,{y}_{1}^{2}+6{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?",
        "worked_solution": "We apply Lagrange's method as follows:\n\nFirst, we group ${x}_{1}^{2}$-term with all cross-product terms that contain ${x}_{1}$ and factor out the coefficient of ${x}_{1}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+38{x}_{2}^{2}+16{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =(2{x}_{1}^{2}+16{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2} & =2([{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+16{x}_{2}^{2}]-16{x}_{2}^{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(({x}_{1}+4{x}_{2})^{2}-16{x}_{2}^{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we simplify the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(({x}_{1}+4{x}_{2})^{2}-16{x}_{2}^{2})+38{x}_{2}^{2} & =2({x}_{1}+4{x}_{2})^{2}-32{x}_{2}^{2}+38{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}+4{x}_{2})^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the canonical form is\n\n$$\n2{y}_{1}^{2}+6{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the missing parts are as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $2\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}.$",
